Description: fftools/ffmpeg_filter: tell agapfill when a rebuilt graph continues an earlier one
 ffmpeg builds a new filter graph when the parameters of the audio
 change mid-stream, for example when an AC-3 stream changes from 5.1 to
 stereo. The agapfill filter of the new graph starts from nothing. With
 its start option it wrote the leading silence a second time, from the
 start time up to the frame at the change. A source of 10.05 s that
 begins at 2 s came out as 19.07 s.
 .
 configure_filtergraph() now sends the command "resume" to every
 agapfill filter of a graph that replaces an earlier one. The filter
 then ignores start and begins at its first frame.
 .
 A gap that falls exactly at such a change is not filled, because the
 new filter does not know where the old one ended. ffmpeg also drops
 the samples that the filters of the old graph still held.
Author: Streamarr
Forwarded: no
