Index: FFmpeg/doc/filters.texi
===================================================================
--- FFmpeg.orig/doc/filters.texi
+++ FFmpeg/doc/filters.texi
@@ -2157,6 +2157,19 @@ agapfill=start=0:max_gap=600
 @end example
 @end itemize
 
+@subsection Commands
+
+This filter supports the following command:
+@table @option
+@item resume
+Tell the filter that its graph continues the output of an earlier graph. The
+filter then ignores @option{start} and begins at its first frame, because the
+earlier graph has already written the leading silence. The command takes no
+argument and has no effect after the first frame. @command{ffmpeg} sends it
+to every agapfill filter of a filter graph that it builds in place of an
+earlier one, for example when the channel layout of the input changes.
+@end table
+
